            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Geoff"
            },
            "reviewBody": "followed the recipe to the letter.the flavor was very tasty, only thing wrong was that I used thawed hamburger,the loaf was very \"wet\" or not firm.even with that,there was'nt much left over.baked mac and cheese accompanied the meal. Will definitely make it again but use fresh not previously frozen ground beef, if that does'nt fix it maybe one more egg and an increase in the breadcrumbs to make it firm. very yummy!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Andra Tobias"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used 1 1/4 lbs. ground turkey instead of the 1 1/2 ground beef ( healthier) and only 1 egg. Most of the reviews read that it didn't hold together well. I'm pretty sure you should only add one egg per lb of meat which is most likely why it is too loose as written, it either needs 2 lbs of meat or 1 egg. I choose the latter. I shaped it into a loaf on a foil-covered cookie sheet (with edges) rather than in a loaf pan. Also I let the meat loaf \"rest\" for about 5 minutes before slicing it. I gave it 5 stars because most meatloaf recipes do not translate well to a turkey meatloaf, but this one was very good as is.",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-04T18:13:32.550Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "fredtabor"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it. Used Piacate sauce instead of salsa and cooked it in my smoker at 275 with a temperature probe so I knew when it was done. Hint: put the meat loaf in the freezer for about 30 min then take it out of the pan, then you can cook it without it sitting in all that grease.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-04T09:12:52.813Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Candi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great flavor! Used a 20 oz. package of ground turkey, 1 egg, and just 2 Tbs of the BBQ sauce and a splash of spicy mustard. Cooked for 1 hour and 15 minutes until the internal temp reached 165. Added shredded cheese on top and placed under the broiler for the last few minutes. Held together just fine! Served with rice and steamed veggies.",
            "datePublished": "2013-03-16T19:35:45.007Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "texjen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have modified this recipe to use ro-tel instead of salsa and more spicy bbq sauce than ketchup in both loaf and cupcake sizes and it's awesome! Pop a little garlic mashed potatoes on top and the cupcakes are a mad hit, plus, you can freeze the naked cupcakes for a quick snack at a later date.",
            "datePublished": "2015-03-10T19:40:14.640Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "akaonyx25"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this meatloaf! I cook it with ground turkey instead of beef. It’s super moist. I would recommend cooking it for 15 minutes longer uncovered to help evaporate the rest of the juices. Other than that I would not change a thing ! Great weekday meal",
            "datePublished": "2020-10-06T00:31:46.373Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JLYNNNAMDG"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this last night for the fam and they ALL loved it! It was nice and moist. I think next time I might only use 1 egg. Also, I omitted the onion since the salsa I used was pretty chunky. I used onion powder (~1tsp.) and garlic powder (~1Tblsp.), also. This is TOTALLY going in my recipe box!",
            "datePublished": "2010-04-17T06:00:32.923Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Deb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "1 1/2 pounds of hamburger does not cook in 1 hr, I usually have to add 20 minutes. I also cut back on the catsup and add 2 Tbl. salsa. Additionally, I use Panko bread crumbs, which helps to not make it so wet.",
            "datePublished": "2015-09-19T12:37:12.103Z"
          },
